<p style="line-height: normal; margin: 0in 0in 8pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif;"><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif; font-size: 19px;"><b><span style="color: black;">Background:</span></b><span style="color: black;"><br>Maria, a 32-year-old mother of two, emigrated from Honduras to the United States five years ago seeking safety from gang violence. She has been living in a mixed-status household—her children are U.S. citizens, but her own immigration status is undocumented. Maria works in housekeeping and has built a supportive network within her local church.</span></span></p>
<p style="line-height: normal; margin: 0in 0in 8pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif;"><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif; font-size: 19px;"><b><span style="color: black;">Situation:</span></b><span style="color: black;"><br>One morning, Maria is detained by Immigration and Customs Enforcement (ICE) during a routine check at her workplace. Her sudden absence leaves her children without their primary caregiver, and her family is at risk of losing their housing due to her lost income. Maria is placed in a detention facility pending deportation proceedings.</span></span></p>
<p><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif; font-size: 19px;"><b><span style="line-height: 115%; color: black;">Generalist Social Work Intervention:</span></b><span style="line-height: 115%; color: black;"><br>A local nonprofit agency assigns a generalist social worker, Alex, to support Maria and her family. Alex follows the generalist practice framework, utilizing engagement, assessment, intervention, and evaluation at multiple levels.</span></span></p>
